      "ownershipVehicle": "Blackstone Energy Transition Partners IV AIV L.P., BXE IV (LUX) AIV SCSp and affiliated vehicles",
      "description": "Hill Top Energy Center is a 620 MW natural-gas combined-cycle power plant in Carmichaels, Pennsylvania that sells energy and capacity into PJM. Ardian Americas Infrastructure Funds acquired a 41.9% co-control interest in July 2019 while the plant was under construction, and the facility entered commercial operation in July 2021. Ardian acquired the remaining interest in April 2025. Blackstone announced a definitive agreement to acquire Hill Top on September 15, 2025, and a direct FERC consummation notice establishes that the transaction closed on March 26, 2026. Hill Top is now indirectly wholly owned through affiliated Blackstone funds, including Blackstone Energy Transition Partners IV AIV L.P. and BXE IV (LUX) AIV SCSp. The FERC record identifies 76.28% and 14.72% aggregator interests for those two vehicles; the internal allocation of the remaining 9% among other affiliated vehicles is not publicly disclosed. The plant company is the canonical PortCo, while buyer and seller holding entities are not counted separately. No later sale or signed pending ownership transfer was identified through August 15, 2026.",
